course: dictionary
lesson: 837
title: Names that are also words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A capital letter often tells you that a word is a name. In «Benjamin Franklin was an American inventor and leader», the capitals show that Benjamin is the name of a real person, not a thing.
explain: The words around a name give clues. In «Benjamin Franklin kept a chart of thirteen virtues and marked his faults every day», the name is followed by what a person did, so it is a person.
explain: Small letters can give a name a different meaning. In US slang, «benjamins» means money, because the 100-dollar bill has Benjamin Franklin's face on it. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is used.
fact: Benjamin is a boy's name, and its short forms are Ben and Benji.
fact: In the Bible, Benjamin was the youngest son of Jacob and the brother of Joseph.
fact: Benjamin Franklin was an American inventor and leader who did experiments with electricity and kites.
fact: Benjamin Franklin invented the lightning rod, which gives lightning an easy metal path down a thick wire into the earth.
fact: In US slang, a benjamin is a 100-dollar bill.
exercise: «Benjamin Franklin was an American inventor and leader.» Is Benjamin a name or a thing? | A kind of kite | A type of cloud | A brand of sweets | *A name, for a real person
exercise: Ben and Benji are short forms of which name? | Franklin | Joseph | Jacob | *Benjamin
exercise: In US slang, what does «benjamins» mean? | A boy's name | A stormy sky | A kind of brother | *Money, a 100-dollar bill
test: «Benjamin Libet's experiments from the 1980s found brain activity before people felt they had decided.» What is Benjamin here? | The word for a decision | A type of brain | *A name of a scientist | A kind of kite
test: In the Bible, who was Benjamin's brother? | Libet | Franklin | Jacob | *Joseph
exam: «A lightning rod gives lightning an easy metal path down a thick wire into the earth, and Benjamin Franklin invented it.» How do we know Benjamin here is a person? | It is a kind of cloud | It means a dollar bill | It rhymes with lightning | *A real person invented something, and his name has a capital letter
